    "diversity_note": "Unique-formula fraction among best-of-n outputs. Selection concentrates the accepted set on the pool's tail near the target, so accuracy and diversity trade against each other in n. The projection shapes the distribution instead of filtering it, so its diversity does not depend on how hard the target is to hit -- which is the axis on which the two approaches actually differ.",
    "cost_note": "Best-of-n costs n forward passes per accepted output, every time, at every target. The projection costs one training run and one forward pass per output. Accuracy alone is therefore not the comparison.",
